Split out of karr #122 rather than folded into it, because it is a decision
about a DIFFERENT slot and it moves ADR 0037s own counter-check table.

MEASURED against sops 3.13.3 at /tmp/sops, with assert_representables
non-finite gate bypassed in a scratch copy of lib/ at HEAD (i.e. WITH
ADR 0037s emit repair in place), unencrypted slot, one document per row:

  YAML, bare 9**9**9 / -9**9**9 / NaN   3 of 3 WRITTEN as .inf / -.inf / .nan,
                                        sops -d exit 0, the leaf a float
  JSON, the same three                  3 of 3 CROAK, from the emit walk
                                        (_non_finite_token_leaf: the JSON
                                        carrier has no token), which is right

So the refusal in assert_representable for a leaf with NO string half of its
own is now redundant in YAML and duplicated in JSON. Its premise -- that the
YAML emitter writes a bare `Inf`, which go-yaml reads as a string -- was
removed by ADR 0037, which teaches _canonical_floats to ask the handlers
carrier for the token. ADR 0031s measurement of this cell (+Inf exit 51,
-Inf/NaN exit 0 with a silently retyped leaf) was taken BEFORE that change and
no longer reproduces.

WHAT IT WOULD COST, measured: the whole thing is one condition
(`_has_public_pv($value) &&` in front of the existing refusal). It flips
8 further subtests beyond karr #122s own -- t/28 sections 1-6 (three YAML rows
become documents, three JSON rows keep refusing with the emit walks message
instead of the guards), t/39 section 11, t/42 section 11, t/46 sections 4-5,
and t/52 section 9, which is ADR 0037s twelve-row encrypt-path counter-check.

WHAT MUST NOT MOVE, and does not in the measurement: every leaf that STATES a
string half its number contradicts -- dualvar(+Inf, banana), dualvar(+Inf,
-.inf), dualvar(+Inf, .INf) -- is written with the callers text and is
sops -d exit 51 (MAC mismatch) if the gate is opened for it too. Those rows
stay refused in every variant measured.

Wire lane. Needs the binary and its own ADR.
